  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Relief  and Life Saving Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the devastating 7.8 magnitude earthquake of March 2025 and amid intensifying military repression, Gaia Green Social Enterprise is delivering emergency humanitarian assistance to the most vulnerable communities in Mandalay and Bago Regions, Myanmar.

Operating under a strict low-profile model, the project will provide Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) to 150 households &#x2014; prioritising women-led families, the elderly, people with disabilities, and those affected by forced conscription &#x2014; enabling them to meet their most urgent survival needs. An additional 250 individuals will receive Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS) through small, discreet group sessions designed to restore wellbeing and resilience.

With an estimated 16 million people nationwide requiring urgent aid in 2026, Gaia&apos;s decentralised, community-rooted approach &#x2014; delivered through trusted local alumni networks using secure channels &#x2014; reaches those international agencies cannot.</narrative>
  </description>
